      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{P}=\\{a,b,c,d,e,f\\}$ and $\\overset{―}{Q}=\\{a,c,e\\},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{P\\cup Q}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{P\\cup Q}≡\\overset{―}{P}\\cap \\overset{―}{Q}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{P\\cup Q} & =\\overset{―}{P}\\cap \\overset{―}{Q} \\\\  & =\\{a,b,c,d,e,f\\}\\cap \\{a,c,e\\} \\\\  & =\\{a,c,e\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
